STILL WAITING; wsj and barrons unchanged at their pre-pin records.

THE RATE DIPPED THIS HOUR AND THE CAUSE IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED. bbg's checkpoint went done 164 ->
179, i.e. 15 jobs against the 21-22 of every previous hour. Reading the inter-job gaps in the log for
07:00-08:41Z: 31 JOB lines, min 2.6 min, MEDIAN 2.7 min, max 17.8 min, and exactly ONE gap over 6
minutes -- 08:07:28Z to 08:25:17Z (17.8 min). So the hour lost about a quarter of itself to ONE long
job and the per-job pace is unchanged at ~2.7 min; this is not a general slowdown and not a stall (the
next job landed normally and the log is current to 08:39:08Z). Nothing was done about it: a single
slow job is inside the normal behaviour of a vendor fetch, and driving the runner is exactly what this
order forbids.
  Remaining 63 of the expected 242: about 2.9 hours at 2.7 min/job, or 4.2 if this hour's 15/hour is
  the new rate. Extrapolation either way.

INSTRUMENT NOTE for anyone re-deriving these numbers: a per-hour count of log LINES is not a count of
JOBS (the 00Z hour shows 263 lines because a cycle start writes a PLAN line per security). The job
counts above come from the checkpoint's own 'done' length and from JOB-filtered log lines, never from
a bare line count.

